{
  "requirement": "Usage MUST record each provider request's outcome and available input/output\ntoken counts, including retries, with cached or reasoning-token counts when\nprovided, and for a failed request the failure under\n{cite}`requirements.authoring.usage_requests.failures`. Missing measurements MUST be recorded as unavailable, not zero.\nRun totals MUST include request and tool-call counts by tool, elapsed time, and\navailable token usage, identifying incomplete totals without double counting\nprovider counters that overlap.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover `requirements.authoring.usage_requests`. I ran one search over `src/authoring/usage.rs` to see how missing counters are recorded.\n\n**Per-request outcome and tokens, including retries**\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[throttled_requests_retry_unchanged_and_record_every_attempt]` has five throttled attempts followed by a success. It asserts `request_count` is 6, every failed attempt has outcome `failed`, and the last has outcome `completed`.\n- `unanswered_requests_are_abandoned_and_retried` checks that an abandoned attempt is recorded as `failed` and the retry as `completed`. `success_resets_backoff_and_retries_keep_history_without_repeating_tools` checks `request_count` is 4 for a run with retries.\n\n**Failure under `usage_requests.failures` (cited)**\n- The throttled-requests test asserts the exact failure record `{http_status: 429, error_code: ThrottlingException, retried: true}` on every failed attempt. It also asserts there is no failure on the final successful request.\n- `usage.rs#mod[tests]/fn[failed_submission_can_be_confirmed_on_a_later_attempt]` asserts `retried` is false at first and true after `retried()`.\n- Neither test checks that failure message text is absent. That is an obligation of the `failures` requirement, not of the subject.\n\n**Cached and reasoning counts when provided**\n- `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` covers cached, cache-creation and reasoning counters per request and in totals.\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[openai_responses_replays_tool_calls_and_records_usage]` asserts cached 6 and reasoning 4 end to end.\n- `claude_requests_carry_cache_checkpoints_and_record_cache_usage` asserts cache read and write per request and in total.\n\n**Missing measurements recorded as unavailable, not zero**\n- `partial_failure_retains_available_totals_and_optional_measurements` asserts a failed request's tokens and an unreported `cached_input` are null.\n- The same test separates a reported `cached_input_tokens(0)`, which totals 0, from an unreported reasoning counter, which stays null.\n- `token_totals_keep_subsets_separate_and_missing_counters_unknown` also asserts null input on the failed request.\n- `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` asserts totals are null when there are no requests.\n- A source read of `end_request` and `TokenCounts::from_usage` showed that a completed request with no counters yields null tokens. `input_metadata_counts_components_and_reads_without_persisting_source` asserts this. It has no `{test}` reference to the subject, but the scenario is exercised.\n\n**Run totals**\n- Tool-call counts by tool: `tool_outcomes_are_distinct_and_unknown_names_do_not_leak_model_text` asserts `tool_call_count` 8 and per-tool counts, failures and skips. The CLI tests assert counts such as `habeas` 3, `list_files` 1 and `submit_judgment` 1.\n- Elapsed time: `completed_requests_and_the_run_record_elapsed_time` checks per-request and run elapsed time, and `cancelled_request_persists_elapsed_time_and_incomplete_totals` checks a cancelled request's elapsed time.\n- Available token usage and incomplete totals: `tokens.complete` is asserted false for an in-flight request, a failed request, a cancelled request and mixed-measurement runs. It is asserted true when all requests are measured.\n- No double counting of overlapping counters: totals for input 200 and output 40 stay unchanged next to cached 60 and reasoning 10. The OpenAI CLI test shows the same (input 22 and output 14 alongside cached 6 and reasoning 4). Bedrock input and output totals of 38 and 10 are asserted in `bedrock_cli_uses_selected_profile_region_and_converse_tools`.\n\nI found no plausible requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "c8b7f08a50b337f9c70d879cbd592e2a60fe6fe78afeca02c2feb559ecfbf2dc",
